          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+bundles"} connections on bundles
            over some prescribed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
          %p
            Often one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+systems"}> local systems
            ) only, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#compactness Compactness
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is compact.
          %h3#over_complex_manifolds__complex_varieties Over complex manifolds / complex varieties
          %p
            Over a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+variety"} complex variety
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul-Malgrange+theorem"} Koszul-Malgrange theorem
            identifies holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            with (a non-abelian version of) the first Griffiths
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobian"} intermediate Jacobian
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobian#ExamplePicard"} intermediate Jacobian – Examples – k=0
          %p
            More specifically over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan%E2%80%93Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan–Seshadri theorem
            identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+flat+connections"} moduli spaces of flat connections
            with that of certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex
            spaces of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundle"} stable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            over that surface. See there for more.
          %p
            More generally, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
            similarly gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+structure"} Kähler structure
            on the moduli space of flat connections also over higher dimensional Kähler manifolds (
            %a{:href => "#ScheinostSchottenloher96"}> Scheinost-Schottenloher 96, corollary 1.16
            ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#FlatConnectionsOverATorus Flat connections over a torus
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
            or is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            (what we really need below is that any two commuting elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            sit jointly in one
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
          %p
            The moduli space of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            on a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \simeq S^1 \times S^1
            (e.g. underlying a complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
          %p
            first, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of flat connections is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi Grp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ×
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi ad
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  [\Pi(A), \mathbf{B}G]
                  \&amp; \simeq [B [A, S^1], \mathbf{B}G]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq Hom_{Grp}(\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}, G)//_{ad} G
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            (see also the discussion at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/group+character#CharactersAndFundamentalGroupsOfTori"} characters and fundamental groups of tori
          %p
            Here a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
            is just a choice of pair of two commuting elements in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts on that by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \hookrightarrow G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugation
            we can take this to be one fixed maximal torus. This means that the moduli space is actually
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ad
                    %mi G
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi W
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0 \left(
                  Hom_{Grp}([A,S^1], G)//_{ad} G
                  \\right)
                  \\simeq
                  Hom_{Grp}([A, S^1], T)/W
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W = N_G(T)/T
          %p
            Moreover, by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+duality"} Pontryagin duality
            this may be re-expressed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi W
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq Hom_{Grp}([T,S^1], A)/W
                  \\,.
          %p
            where now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T,S^1]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character+group"} character group
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
          %p
            In this form the moduli space of flat connections appears prominently for instance in the discussion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            is at least more subtle, see (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie15"}> Lurie 15
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tamagawa+numbers"} Tamagawa numbers
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+complex+structures"} moduli space of complex structures
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+conformal+structures"} moduli space of conformal structures
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+curves"} moduli space of curves
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Riemannian+metrics"} moduli space of Riemannian metrics
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Calabi-Yau+spaces"} moduli space of Calabi-Yau spaces
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+tori"} moduli stack of tori
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+formal+groups"} moduli stack of formal groups
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+connections"}> moduli space of connections
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+moduli+space"} Hitchin moduli space
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+framed+manifolds"} moduli space of framed manifolds
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+bundles"} moduli space of bundles
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+%28higher%29+line+bundles"} moduli space of (higher) line bundles
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+variety"} quiver variety
          %h2#references References
          %p Original articles include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Yang-Mills equations over Riemann surfaces
              %p
                Vol. 308, No. 1505 (Mar. 17, 1983), pp. 523-615 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/37156"}> jstor
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/295505/58526"} lighning summary
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> Nigel Hitchin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
            %li
              %p
                Nan-Kuo Ho, Chiu-Chu Melissa Liu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the connectedness of moduli spaces of flat connections over compact surfaces
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-2004-053-3"} doi
          %p
            Review and lecture notes, mostly for the case of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Remi Janner,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on the moduli space of flat connections
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/265223952_Notes_on_the_moduli_space_of_flat_connections"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Daan Michiels,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Moduli spaces of flat connections
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~Schat001/Daan_thesis.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Teschner14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B6rg+Teschner"}> Jörg Teschner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantization of moduli spaces of flat connections and Liouville theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0359"} arXiv:1405.0359
            %li#FockGoncharov14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+V.+Fock"}> Vladimir V. Fock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Alexander G. Goncharov
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Alexander+G.+Goncharov"} ?
                %em Symplectic double for moduli spaces of G-local systems on surfaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1410.3526"}> arXiv:1410.3526
                )
          %p
            and for the case of general and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithmic+connections"} logarithmic connections
          %ul
            %li#BiswasMunoz
              Indranil Biswas, V.Munoz,
              %em Moduli spaces of connections on a Riemann surface
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mat.ucm.es/~vmunozve/Moduli.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Introcuction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fock-Goncharov+coordinates"} Fock-Goncharov coordinates
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+flat+connections"} moduli spaces of flat connections
          %ul
            %li#FockGoncharov06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+V.+Fock"}> Vladimir V. Fock
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+B.+Goncharov"} Alexander B. Goncharov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Moduli spaces of local systems and higher Teichmüller theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 103
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0311149"} arXiv:math/0311149
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10240-006-0039-4"} doi:10.1007/s10240-006-0039-4
          %p Detailed discussion of moduli space of flat connections also on higher dimensional base spaces is in
          %ul
            %li#ScheinostSchottenloher96
              Peter Scheinost,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
              = succeed "," do
                %em Metaplectic quantization of the moduli spaces of flat and parabolic bundles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/153753"} web
          %p
            For more references see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Lurie15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/226716/381"} MO comment
              2015
